  "chapter": {
    "number": 48,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(49) For the end, a Psalm for the sons of Core."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hear these words, all you⌃ nations, listen, all you⌃ that dwell upon the earth:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "both the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 88
          },
          {
            "text": "sons of mean men, and sons of great men; the rich and poor man together.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My mouth shall speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart shall bring forth understanding.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will incline my ear to a parable: I will open my",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 89
          },
          {
            "text": "riddle on the harp.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 90
          },
          {
            "text": "should I fear in the evil day? the iniquity of my heel shall compass me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They that trust in their strength, and boast themselves in the multitude of their wealth—",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A brother does not redeem, shall a man redeem? he shall not give to God a ransom for himself,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "or the price of the redemption of his soul, though he labor for ever,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and live to the end, so that he should not see corruption.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When he shall see wise men dying, the fool and the senseless one shall perish together; and they shall leave their wealth to strangers.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And their sepulchres are their houses for ever, even their tabernacles to all generations: they have called their lands after their own names.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And man being in honor, understands not: he is compared to the senseless cattle, and is like to them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "This their way is an offense to them: yet afterwards men will commend their sayings. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have laid them as sheep in Hades; death shall feed on them; and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning, and their help shall fail in Hades from their glory.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But God shall deliver my soul from the power of Hades, when he shall receive me. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Fear not when a man is enriched, and when the glory of his house is increased.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he shall take nothing when he dies; neither shall his glory descend with him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For his soul shall be blessed in his life: he shall give thanks to you when you do well to him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yet he shall go in",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 91
          },
          {
            "text": "to the generation of his fathers; he shall never see light.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Man that is in honor, understands not: he is compared to the senseless cattle, and is like them.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
